{"shortDescription":"Fund managers have shifted their primary market worry. Bank of America’s September Global Fund Manager Survey, which polled 170 investors overseeing $470B in assets now ranks a disorderly rise in bond yields as the top tail risk.A total of 33% of the respondents cited yields as the top tail risk. T…","astDescription":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Fund managers have shifted their primary market worry. Bank of America’s September Global Fund Manager Survey, which polled 170 investors overseeing $470B in assets now ranks a disorderly rise in bond yields as the top tail risk."]},{"type":"p","children":["A total of 33% of the respondents cited yields as the top tail risk. That reading is up from 27% in August and knocks last month’s leader—an AI bubble—down to 28% from 32%."]},{"type":"p","children":["The change marks the first time this year that yield instability has outranked AI concerns in the monthly poll. A second wave of inflation still registered with 24% of managers. Geopolitical conflict, a Democratic sweep in the U.S. midterms, and dollar debasement trailed far behind at 6%, 5%, and 2%, respectively."]},{"type":"p","children":["The reordering of risks arrives as global yields have climbed to multiyear highs, with the U.S. 10-Year Treasury yield ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"TVC:US10Y","text":"TVC:US10Y"}}," recently pushing ",{"type":"url","params":{"url":"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4642526-us-10-year-tops-5-for-the-first-time-since-october-of-2023?utm_source=tradingview\u0026utm_medium=referral\u0026feed_item_type=news","linkText":"above 5%"}},"."]},{"type":"p","children":["BofA’s long-running survey treats tail risks as low-probability events with outsized impact. The latest results suggest institutions are more focused on a sudden repricing of duration than on a collapse in the AI trade—even as crowded semiconductor positioning remains a separate, closely watched theme."]},{"type":"p","children":[{"type